  "built:0#v2": {
   "output": {
    "decisions": [
     {
      "id": "DEC-01",
      "path": "src/gateway.js",
      "line": 4,
      "why": "The fetch call on line 4 passes only method and body (lines 5-6). It has no signal or AbortSignal.timeout, so nothing limits the call to 5 s and a slow gateway can hang. The catch on lines 10-11 returns PENDING for errors, but no line sets the 5 s timeout the decision requires. The behaviour is missing.",
      "verdict": "not_built"
     },
     {
      "id": "DEC-02",
      "path": "src/refund-service.js",
      "line": 13,
      "why": "Line 13 returns the stored result when the order ID is already in the store, so a repeat refund does not reach the gateway again. The store read on line 13 and the IN_PROGRESS write on line 15 both run before postRefund on line 16, so a store failure throws before anything is sent to the gateway, as the decision says.",
      "verdict": "built"
     }
    ]
   },
